      "notes": "Upstream shared one persistent browser context across the file, slept (waitForTimeout) instead of waiting for the event the spec is named after, and drew the OSMTILE extent from server.arcgisonline.com. Now each test loads its own page (D4), the switch sets the public projection property and waits for map-projectionchange (so the extents' disabled state is asserted when the event fires, which is what MapML.js defers the event for), and the OSMTILE extent uses the local test tiles (D8); the fixture's changeProjection() script is gone. Tagged @CBMTILE (it is about the OSMTILE to CBMTILE switch), so MapML-MapLibre skips it. Upstream's skipped 'History is empty' test passes on MapML.js and MapML-OpenLayers and now runs: it moves the map first (reload enabled) so the history reset is actually tested, and finds reload by its contract testid and role instead of getByLabel('Reload'). MapML-OpenLayers test/projection-switch.test.js stays pending: it covers centre/scale preservation, matchMedia and layer state, which belong to core/projectionChange.test.js."
