    "core/announceMovement.test.js": {
      "status": "converted",
      "notes": "Upstream CBMTILE scenario runs unchanged on upstream fixtures (@CBMTILE), and again in OSMTILE on new counterparts announceMovementMapmlViewer.html / announceMovementWebMap.html (layer min zoom 2, sized so the moves hold for keyboard pan steps of 80-128px), each for <mapml-viewer> and <map is=\"web-map\">. The second test used to start where the first left off; it now replays those moves (D4). The live region is found by class (CONTRACT.md, new section), and every announcement is recorded by a MutationObserver, so key presses are followed until an announcement ending \"zoom level N\" instead of fixed sleeps, and transient bound messages are checked deterministically. Added: the region is role=status aria-live=polite aria-atomic=true, Tab lands on zoom-in-button before Enter, and a bounced pan restores lon (moved in from both port tests, now deleted). Fixed MapML-OpenLayers: keyboard pan/zoom was dead on <map is=web-map> (OL only accepts keys targeted at its target shadow host, the inner div; web-map now forwards the <map>s keydowns). Fixed MapML-MapLibre: after bouncing back into bounds it never re-announced \"zoom level N\" (upstream asserts it; MapML.js announces the last moveend of a traversal).",
